/*
 * ComsolToroidLossless.java -- COMSOL Multiphysics model generated by axionFEM (python/axionfem/comsol.py).
 *
 * axionFEM design: comsol_toroid_lossless  (3D; lengths in metres)
 * Region selections reproduce axionFEM's painting order (later regions win) with Difference selections;
 * '<region>_boundary' are the adjacent boundaries; 'all_superconductors' / 'all_conductors' group regions by kind.
 * pickup: {"port": "port", "type": "port"}
 * approximation: ports: axionFEM feeds the current through the gap volume (Laplace profile); the COMSOL LumpedPort carries it on one face of the gap, a modelling difference of order (gap size / loop size)
 *
 * PHYSICS (--physics fullwave): Electromagnetic Waves, Frequency Domain (emw), exp(+j omega t): complex values are
 *   the complex conjugates of axionFEM's (exp(-i omega t)); axionFEM Z = R - i omega L, COMSOL Z = R + j omega L.
 *   frequencies [MHz]: 1, 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 40, 50, 60; outer boundary: pec (axionFEM fullwave.boundary)
 *   ports: 1 = pickup (port)
 *   axion source Je = Je_scale*B0: fullwave.source toroidal_box: B_phi = 1.0 T for rho in [0.525, 0.975] m, z in [-0.225, 0.225] m, 0 outside (exact)
 *   main(): 'imp' run (port 1 driven, Je off) -> Zport_1; 'volt' run (Je on, port 1 not driven, so loaded by its
 *   reference impedance, 50 ohm by default) -> Vport_1. Open-circuit V = Vport (Zport + Z_ref)/Z_ref.
 *   Calls marked UNVERIFIED are not in the COMSOL 6.4 template this export copies (docs/comsol_export.md).
 *
 * Build and run (needs the RF Module for emw/LumpedPort; main() solves the imp and volt runs and writes ComsolToroidLossless_impedance.txt / ComsolToroidLossless_voltage.txt to the working directory):
 *   comsolcompile ComsolToroidLossless.java                  # -> ComsolToroidLossless.class
 *   comsol batch -inputfile ComsolToroidLossless.class       # -> comsol_toroid_lossless.mph
 * or open ComsolToroidLossless.class with File > Open in the COMSOL Desktop.
 * See docs/comsol_export.md.
 */
